   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 187 of the laws of 1960 incorporating the West Islip\nExempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, in relation to its purpose and the\nuse of foreign fire insurance premium taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S7555",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7555-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2, 3 & 7, Chap 187 of 1960",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Assoc., Inc.",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7555\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 187 of the laws of 1960 incorporating the West\nIslip Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, in relation to its\npurpose and the use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 187 of the laws of 1960 incorporating the West\nIslip Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, in relation to its\npurpose and the use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Sections 1, 2, 3 and 7 of chapter 187 of the laws of 1960\nincorporating the West Islip Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association,\nare amended to read as follows: Section 1.  Incorporation; membership. A\n \nMEMBERSHIP not-for-profit corporation by the name of \"West Islip\nExempt  \nFIREMEN'S Firefighter's Benevolent Association\" is hereby\ncreated. It shall be composed of such persons eligible to membership\ntherein as hereinafter provided as shall(a) notify the secretary of the\nWest Islip fire department in writing prior to the organization meeting\nof such corporation hereinafter provided for their desire to become\nmembers, or (b) shall attend such meeting or an adjournment thereof, and\nalso such persons so eligible as may become members of such corporation\npursuant to its by-laws. § 2. Persons eligible to membership. All\npersons who are now, or have been, or who hereafter shall be volunteer\nmembers of the West Islip fire district fire department, or of any fire\ncorporation in such fire district, and all persons resident in such fire\ndistrict or in territory provided with fire protection by contract with\nsuch fire district who are exempt volunteer  \nFIREMEN firefighters as\ndefined by section  \nTWO HUNDRED 200 of the general municipal law, shall\nbe eligible to membership in the corporation hereby created; provided\nthat any person who has been expelled or removed for cause from member-\nship in any fire company or department shall not be eligible to member-\nship in such corporation.  Whenever a member who is not an exempt  \nFIRE-\nMAN firefighter as defined by section  \nTWO HUNDRED 200 of the general\nmunicipal law shall remove from such fire district or from territory\nprovided with fire protection as aforesaid or if the territory in which\na member resides shall no longer be provided with such fire protection,\n \nHIS such person's membership in such corporation shall cease. 04/29/24\n3 15320-01-4 § 3. Purposes. The purposes of such corporation shall be\n \nTHE MAINTENANCE OF SUITABLE HEADQUARTERS FOR, AND THE PROMOTION OF\nFRATERNAL INTERCOURSE AMONG THE MEMBERS OF SUCH CORPORATION, THE RELIEF,\nAID AND ASSISTANCE OF SUCH MEMBERS AND THEIR FAMILIES WHO ARE DISABLED\nOR INDIGENT, AND THE PROMOTION OF THE WELFARE OF THE VOLUNTEER FIRE\nSERVICE WITHIN THE.WEST ISLIP FIRE DISTRICT AND TERRITORY PROVIDED WITH\nFIRE PROTECTION BY CONTRACT WITH SUCH FIRE DISTRICT:to provide relief,\naid and assistance to the volunteer members of such corporation who are\ndisabled, indigent or injured in the performance of their duties, and\ntheir families; to promote and safeguard the welfare of the volunteer\nmembers of such corporation, and their families; to maintain a suitable\nheadquarters for the members of such corporation; to provide for the\nhealth and safety of the volunteer members of such corporation; include\nsupport for mental health and encourage team building skills in order to\nstrengthen the safety among the volunteers, and the promotion of the\nvolunteer fire service with in the territory protected by the West Islip\nfire district fire department. § 7. Precept for payment of foreign fire\ninsurance premium taxes. Such corporation shall collect and there shall\nbe paid to it all taxes imposed by section  \nFIVE HUNDRED FIFTY-THREE)\n9104 OF THE INSURANCE LAW, FOR FIRE DEPARTMENT USE AND BENEFIT, UPON\nPREMIUMS FOR INSURANCE AGAINST LOSS OR DAMAGE BY FIRE COVERING PROPERTY\nSITUATED WITHIN THE TERRITORY PROTECTED BY THE WEST ISLIP FIRE DEPART-\nMENT, LOCATED IN THE TOWN OF ISLIP, SUFFOLK COUNTY, NEW YORK, OR WITHIN\nANY DULY ORGANIZED TERRITORY IN WHICH THE WEST ISLIP FIRE DEPARTMENT IS\nOR MAY BE OBLIGATED TO RENDER FIRE PROTECTION. THE OFFICER OF SAID\nCORPORATION DESIGNATED BY ITS BYLAWS TO COLLECT AND RECEIVE THE AFORE-\nSAID TAX SHALL HAVE ALL THE POWERS AND BE SUBJECT TO ALL THE PROVISIONS\nOF THE INSURANCE LAW, RELATING TO TREASURERS OF FIRE DEPARTMENTS. SUCH\nCORPORATION SHALL ALSO BE ENTITLED TO RECEIVE A SHARE OF THE TAX IMPOSED\nBY SECTION  \nFIVE HUNDRED FIFTY-FOUR 9105 OF THE INSURANCE LAW, BASED\nUPON THE BUSINESS WRITTEN IN THE TERRITORY WITH RESPECT TO WHICH IT IS\nENTITLED TO COLLECT AND RECEIVE THE TAX UNDER SECTION  \nFIVE HUNDRED\nFIFTY-THREE) 9104 OF THE INSURANCE LAW. SUCH TAXES SHALL ONLY BE USED\n \nFOR THE CARE AND RELIEF OF DISABLED OR INDIGENT VOLUNTEER AND EXEMPT\nVOLUNTEER FIREMEN AND THEIR FAMILIES) BY THE CORPORATION IN FURTHERANCE\nOF ITS PURPOSES AS SET FORTH IN SECTION THREE OF THIS ACT.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFIREFIGHTERS PUT THEIR LIFE ON THE LINE EVERY DAY AND RISK THEIR LIVES\nTO PROTECT THE PEOPLE FROM A FIRE. THE PURPOSE OF THIS BILL IS TO\nPROVIDE RELIEF, AID AND ASSISTANCE TO THE VOLUNTEER MEMBERS OF SUCH\nCORPORATION WHO ARE DISABLED, INDIGENT OR INJURED IN THE PERFORMANCE OF\nTHEIR DUTIES, AND THEIR FAMILIES; TO PROMOTE AND SAFEGUARD THE WELFARE\nOF THE VOLUNTEER MEMBERS OF SUCH CORPORATION, AND THEIR FAMILIES; TO\nMAINTAIN A SUITABLE HEADQUARTERS FOR THE MEMBERS OF SUCH CORPORATION; TO\nPROVIDE FOR THE HEALTH AND SAFETY OF THE VOLUNTEER MEMBERS OF SUCH\nCORPORATION; INCLUDE SUPPORT FOR MENTAL HEALTH AND ENCOURAGE TEAM BUILD-\nING SKILLS IN ORDER TO STRENGTHEN THE SAFETY AMONG THE VOLUNTEERS, AND\nTHE PROMOTION OF THE VOLUNTEER FIRE SERVICE WITH IN THE TERRITORY\nPROTECTED BY THE WEST ISLIP FIRE DISTRICT FIRE DEPARTMENT.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024: A.10005 REPORTED REFERRED TO RULES\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNONE.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nTHIS ACT SHALL TAKE EFFECT IMMEDIATELY; PROVIDED, HOWEVER, THAT THE\nAMENDMENTS TO SECTION 7 OF CHAPTER 187 OF THE LAWS OF 1960 MADE BY\nSECTION ONE OF THIS ACT SHALL APPLY TO TAXES DUE ON PREMIUMS RECEIVED ON\nAND AFTER JANUARY 1, 2025.\n",
